A||||3||NEFA||NEFA 2001 Leaf Peepers Tour This weekend!!||||7||
Z||000000||NEFA||10-11-2001||03:32 PM||||The New England Fiero Association cordially invites you to attend our 2nd Annual "Leaf Peeper's Tour" on Saturday, October 13th, 2001 leaving from the parking lot of the Old Farms Hotel in Avon, CT <BR>(http://www.avonoldfarmshotel.com). Plan to meet at 9:30 am, as the cruise starts promptly at 10:00 am. Travel with us as we wind our way  up, in, and through the mountains of Western Mass., concluding the <BR>cruise at the Yankee Candle Factory and Auto Museum in South Deerfield, MA (http://www.yankeecandle.com). All are welcome and encouraged to cruise with us, and I look forward to seeing everyone there!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/nefa_logo.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/calendar.htm" TARGET=_blank>Upcoming Club Events</A> <P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/tshirt.html" TARGET=_blank>Get your Club T-shirt</A>||||reg||7
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||10-11-2001||05:02 PM||||Can't wait  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Hope to see lots of New Englanders  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">    <BR>:D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000002||Fiero5||10-12-2001||01:38 PM||||OK, I am having to pull a lot of strings here to possibly be able to go. As it looks like right now, it will be two Fieros from the Kelley clan. Marian will stay behind to do the soccer thing and my Dad (and his 87GT), my daughter Tarrah and I (in probably Fiero9) will be cruising to CT.<P>I hope that we can see a large turnout of Fiero owners, as this will probably be the last big Fiero event in our area for this year. Whether you are in a club or not, we would love to have you as this is open to all Fiero enthusiasts. We all agree that we have a great time driving and showing off our Fieros. With the great leaf colors that are out there right now as most areas are reaching peak color as we speak, we have the ingredients for having nothing but tons of fun. We will enjoy some great foliage sight seeing along the way, tons of photo opportunities with all our Fieros and the beautiful backdrop of all the fall colors. Added the Yankee Candle factory at the end and we have the mixture for an awesome day.<P>Hope to see lots of you Fiero nuts there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Steve||||reg||6
Z||000003||tomcat06085||10-12-2001||06:21 PM||||Hey guys....maybe next event. A slight delay has held up delivery of the 88 GT that I'm buying from New Jersey. Avon Old Farms was where my son and daughter in law had their wedding reception. I live about ten minutes away from Avon Old Farms, but have to skip this one. The GT should be ready for autocrossing next spring though...its road worthy but won't be here till next week more than likely. The leaves and weather is great for tomorrow...today was low 70's and sunny...beautiful day like that tomorrow. Have a great time though.<P><P>------------------<BR>tomcat<BR>Help me go fast!||||reg||7
